"""Align maintained behavior documentation with the 0.87.0 implementation."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
def edit(name,old,new):
 p=ROOT/name;s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');assert old in s,name;s=s.replace(old,new,1);p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
guide='docs/ARTIST_GUIDE.md'
edit(guide,'**Image / pattern density** and **Mesh-channel density** are independent.','**Image / pattern density** and **Surface density** are independent.')
edit(guide,'Map accepts a compatible texture output such as Bitmap or Noise and enables **Use image** when a map is chosen. Cyrus evaluates a 2D tile; a complete surface material is not a scalar mask.', 'Map enables **Use image** and selects **Map coordinates**, evaluating the graph on each receiving surface. Supported graphs include Vertex Color, Color Correction, Output, Checker, Bitmap, Mix, Noise, RGB Multiply and Gradient. A Vertex Color node can read its own data channel, and Checker can read its own UV channel; nested outputs retain that context. A complete material is not a scalar density map. Renderer/camera-dependent maps and unsupported classes report an error.')
edit(guide,'Only UV mode requires receiver UVs.','Projected World/Scatter-local images do not require UVs. Receiver UV needs the selected UV channel; Map coordinates needs each channel requested by its graph.')
edit(guide,'Map resolution 64/128/256/512 controls sampled detail independently of physical tile size. Image mapping controls appear when **Use image** is enabled; mesh-channel controls appear when **Use mesh channel** is enabled.','Map resolution 64/128/256/512 controls projected image detail independently of physical tile size. Map coordinates samples the graph directly at each candidate; it is not a raster bake. Image mapping controls appear when **Use image** is enabled. Surface field controls appear when **Use surface field** is enabled. **Clear** removes the assigned map and disables image density, while retaining the independent surface field. Disabling Use image alone keeps the map for later re-enabling. Choosing an Image or pattern restores World XY; choosing Map restores Map coordinates.')
edit(guide,'For portable Save, use a supported static RGB/RGBA PNG or explicitly **Bake portable snapshot**:', 'Arbitrary procedural graphs are retained in Max scenes but are not serialized by the portable package adapter. Receiver-aware graphs cannot be baked into a context-free tile. For projected image workflows, portable Save accepts a supported static RGB/RGBA PNG or explicit **Bake portable snapshot**:')
edit(guide,'**Mesh channel density** reads numeric values directly from each receiving','**Surface density > Mesh channel** reads numeric values directly from each receiving')
edit(guide,'Enable **Use mesh channel** in Amount. Choose','Enable **Use surface field** in Amount and choose **Mesh channel**. Choose')
edit(guide,'For terrain curvature, put Data Channel', '**Relative elevation** is the other surface field. It measures evaluated receiver-local Z from 0 at the lowest referenced vertex to 1 at the highest; a flat receiver is 0. It creates no channel or modifier. Invert and the response curve control low/high planting. Node translation, rotation and scale preserve this local field. The revised Valley and Mountain presets use this mode, so they require neither a fabricated channel 2 nor the original scene altitude. Explicit artist-authored channels remain requirements.\n\nFor terrain curvature, put Data Channel')
edit(guide,'Map samples are reused while the map, its resolution and its evaluation interval\nremain valid. Receiver/UV changes can reuse the bake.', 'Projected image samples are reused while the map, its resolution and its evaluation interval\nremain valid. Receiver/UV changes can reuse that bake. Receiver-aware maps re-evaluate relevant receiver/channel/graph changes; unrelated animation and idle do not sample or solve.')
edit(guide,'Missing mesh-channel data and incompatible Paint are explained before adding anything; no saved terrain is substituted. Static paths retain authored dimensions relative to the saved terrain frame.', 'Explicit missing mesh-channel requirements are explained before adding anything; no saved terrain is substituted. Complete presets transfer Paint contours and path positions from the saved local-XY footprint into the destination footprint. Plant sizes, spacing, brush radius, falloff and path widths convert system units and retain physical dimensions. Paint supports single-valued local-XY terrain; closed, folded or stacked projections reject before import. Original Paint is preserved. Settings-only exact Paint restoration still requires its compatible receiver.')
edit(guide,'Models are source scene objects.', 'Removing the last model produces a valid empty layer after Update in Manual, or automatically in Live. Amount changes remain valid while empty, and adding a replacement resumes normal validation. A failed update retains the last complete result; intentionally empty output clears it.\n\nModels are source scene objects.')
workflow='docs/plans/preset-gallery-improvements/ARTIST_WORKFLOW.md'
edit(workflow,'# Cyrus Library — 0.86.2 workflow','# Cyrus Library — 0.87.0 workflow')
edit(workflow,'The [current delivery report](DELIVERY_0862.md) owns package identities, qualification and limits.', 'The [0.87.0 reliability ledger](RELIABILITY_0870.md) owns current qualification progress and limits. The [0.86.2 report](DELIVERY_0862.md) preserves its older-host deliveries.')
edit(workflow,'Browsing reads saved metadata and images.', 'Pressing **Recipes** restores a minimized Library to its normal size and brings the existing window forward. Closing with X and opening Recipes creates a normal window. Opening Recipes for a different setup or selected receiver updates the captured destination and invalidates callbacks from the previous destination. Windows can restrict foreground activation when another application is active.\n\nBrowsing reads saved metadata and images.')
edit(workflow,'Missing numeric channels or incompatible receiver-bound Paint are reported before scene mutation. Paint requires matching evaluated geometry, frame and saved system units. Static spline paths transfer relative to the saved terrain frame while retaining authored dimensions; this is not arbitrary reprojection or fit-to-bounds scaling.', 'Explicit missing numeric channels are reported before scene mutation. Complete presets fit saved Paint contours and spline guide positions from the saved local-XY footprint to the selected footprint. Units convert automatically; plant size, spacing, brush radius, falloff and path widths keep physical dimensions. Paint requires a single-valued local-XY receiver; closed, folded or stacked projections fail with a useful explanation. Source coverage remains unchanged. Settings-only exact Paint restoration retains its original compatibility checks.')
edit(workflow,'automatic arbitrary-terrain Paint transfer','Paint transfer onto folded or stacked local-XY surfaces')
edit(workflow,'The [current delivery report](DELIVERY_0862.md) links the qualified matching-host MZPs and unsigned Windows EXE for Max 2024/2026/2027.', 'The new 0.87.0 delivery targets Max 2027. Run its verified MZP through **Scripting > Run Script**, then restart Max 2027. The [earlier delivery report](DELIVERY_0862.md) retains the distinct Max 2024/2026/2027 MZPs and Windows EXE.')
edit(workflow,'The [artist guide](../../ARTIST_GUIDE.md) owns image mapping, Show/Hide mask and explicit portable snapshots.', 'The [artist guide](../../ARTIST_GUIDE.md) owns projected image mapping, receiver-aware procedural maps, Show/Hide mask and explicit portable snapshots. Receiver-aware graphs use their own UV/data channels and remain editable in Max scenes; arbitrary graph export is outside the portable adapter. Valley and Mountain use relative local elevation without original-scene channel/altitude dependencies.')
cap='docs/Current_System_2026-10-05/CAPABILITY_MATRIX.md';p=ROOT/cap;lines=p.read_text().splitlines()
for i,line in enumerate(lines):
 if line.startswith('| C11 |'):lines[i]='| C11 | Density masks / layer | Independent projected image, receiver-aware procedural map and surface fields. Map coordinates supplies actual receiver UV/data channels to supported graphs. Surface field chooses explicit channel 0..99 or relative local elevation. Shared bounded placement/preview scalars; Clear removes only the image rule | No map/channel enrollment or write contract | [0.87.0 scoped qualification](../plans/preset-gallery-improvements/RELIABILITY_0870.md); supported classes and resource limits in [format 7](../plans/preset-gallery-improvements/FORMAT_7.md). No arbitrary procedural graph portability or renderer context |'
 if line.startswith('| C35 |'):lines[i]='| C35 | Settings presets and complete static recipes | Multi-layer recipes retain supported Paint/assets/paths, revisions, thumbnails, image bytes/mapping/frame/response and selective style. Selected-terrain Load creates a setup only when needed and adds layers. Complete preset Paint/path transfer fits local XY, with physical unit conversion and early dependency checks | Catalog help only; no preset/recipe filesystem or application tool | Recipe 7, settings 3, library 4, asset capability/graph 2 (manifest 1). One Undo/Redo restores output/assets. Folded/stacked Paint receivers reject; settings-only exact Paint keeps its compatibility contract. Broader Edit/effects/animation/XRef/renderer adapters remain outside scope. See [0.87.0](../plans/preset-gallery-improvements/RELIABILITY_0870.md) |'
